Improved REST API performance for responses containing nested Location representations (e.g. `?depth=1` device lists) by caching `Location.natural_key_field_lookups`, which previously performed a config lookup — a cache-backend round-trip — for every serialized object. The cache is invalidated on Location tree-shape changes and on changes to `LOCATION_NAME_AS_NATURAL_KEY`, the same events that already invalidate the generic natural-key lookup cache.
